    "result_text": "The test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `customerCode`, `namesakeCount`, etc.), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, backed by a helper `membershipNumber(Owner)` that returns `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`. It's derived at read time from the owner's own fields (matching how `displayName`/`initials` are already computed), and returns `null` when either `customerCode` or `registrationDate` is absent \u2014 this guards seed owners (which have null customer code / registration date) from NPEs in `listOwners`.\n\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` checkpoint passes).",
